da)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Exploring_st-_john%27s_antigua_-_5.jpg/960px-Exploring_st-_john%27s_antigua_-_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Antigua Recreation Ground","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.122222,"lo":-61.839167,"d":959,"ds":"Antigua Recreation Ground is the national stadium of Antigua and Barbuda. It is located in St. John's, on the island of Antigua.","wpu":"Antigua Recreation Ground","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Antigua_Recreation_Ground_WI_v_A_2003_001.jpg/960px-Antigua_Recreation_Ground_WI_v_A_2003_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Victoria Park Botanical Gardens","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.120064,"lo":-61.837975,"d":1151,"ds":"The Victoria Park Botanical Gardens (VPBG) is a 5.9-acre (2.4 ha) botanical garden in St. John's, Antigua and Barbuda. It is also home to the Government Complex, the seat of the government of Antigua and Barbuda which contains the parliament building, the prime minister's office, and the high court.","wpu":"Victoria Park Botanical Gardens","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Botanical_Garden_%285915535835%29.jpg/960px-Botanical_Garden_%285915535835%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Diocese of Saint John's–Basseterre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.116111,"lo":-61.837778,"d":1396,"ds":"The Diocese of Saint John's–Basseterre (Latin: Dioecesis Sancti Ioannis–Imatellurana) is a diocese of the Latin Church of the Catholic Church, covering five English-speaking jurisdictions in the Caribbean. The bishopric is a suffragan of the Metropolitan Archdiocese of Castries, and a member of the Antilles Episcopal Conference, but remains dependent on the missionary Dicastery for Evangelization.","wpu":"Diocese of Saint John's–Basseterre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Basseterre_Co-Cathedral_of_Immaculate_Conception.JPG/960px-Basseterre_Co-Cathedral_of_Immaculate_Conception.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"McKinnon's Pond","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.146,"lo":-61.852,"d":2482,"ds":"McKinnon's Pond is located just north of St. John's, Antigua and Barbuda, the largest city in the country. Runaway Beach is just west of it, and it is fed by a small stream leading from St.","wpu":"McKinnon's Pond","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/McKinnon%27s_Salt_Pond.jpg/960px-McKinnon%27s_Salt_Pond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Dickenson Bay Division","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.145,"lo":-61.857222,"d":2532,"ds":"Dickenson Bay is a division of Saint John, Antigua and Barbuda. It is composed of towns such as Trade Winds, McKinnon's, and Blue Waters, some of the most premier resort areas on the island's north coast. McKinnon's Pond is the largest body of water in the area and several ghauts flow into it.","wpu":"Dickenson Bay Division","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Dickenson_Bay_Division.svg/960px-Dickenson_Bay_Division.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Johnston, St. John's","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.119342,"lo":-61.816386,"d":3399,"ds":"St. Johnston (or St. Johnston Village) is a settlement in the northwest of the island of Antigua.","wpu":"St. Johnston, St. John's","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/St._Johnston_map.svg/960px-St._Johnston_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Big Creek Bridge (Antigua)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.092186,"lo":-61.848944,"d":3538,"ds":"Big Creek Bridge is a bridge located in western Antigua spanning Cooks Creek, the boundary between the parishes of Saint John and Saint Mary. It replaced the adjacent Old Big Creek Bridge which was abandoned following an earthquake in 1974. It carries Valley Road, the main link to the southwestern coast of the island.","wpu":"Big Creek Bridge (Antigua)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Big_Creek_Bridge.jpg/960px-Big_Creek_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tomlinson House (Antigua)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":17.114578,"lo":-61.815181,"d":3641,"ds":"Tomlinson House is a historical site of Antigua and Barbuda and a former sugar estate located in Tomlinson. Under Vere Bird, the house was the official residence of the prime minister of Antigua and Barbuda. The sugar estate was established in 1708.","wpu":"Tomlinson House (Antigua)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tomlinson_House%2C_Antigua.jpg/960px-Tomlinson_House%2C_Antigua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"St. John's (Antiguan and Barbudan Creole: Sen Jaan) is the largest city in Antigua and Barbuda. It is located in the western part of Antigua, surrounding St.","wpu":"St. John's, Antigua and Barbuda","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/St_Johns_Antigua_2012.jpg/960px-St_Johns_Antigua_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}